            <ArticleTitle>The use of hypnosis in the management of preoperative anxiety and postoperative pain in a patient undergoing laminectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>143-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients undergoing laminectomy face a variety of concerns both pre- and postoperatively which may affect their emotional state and increase surgical risk. A case study of a laminectomy patient who was taught hypnosis for the control of preoperative anxiety and postoperative pain is presented. The benefits of such hypnotic intervention, as well as the long-term effects of hypnotic intervention on a patient who is in a crisis period are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
